## Actual project goal

ConstraintBox is intended to be a deterministic, Python-based, SMT/constraint-oriented harness around LLM work.

Models propose, explore, interpret, paraphrase, criticize, and fill declared files. Deterministic CB code:

- validates input and output structures;
- chooses only from declared operations;
- launches workers through controlled routes;
- records provider and parentage evidence;
- applies finite gates;
- controls retries and cancellation;
- accepts or rejects return artifacts;
- appends authoritative state;
- generates a compact human-facing result from actual evidence.

The project is specifically trying to reduce common LLM failures:

- narrative completion substituted for work;
- self-report used as proof;
- context rot and recency bias;
- prompt collapse into one interpretation;
- fake agent spawning;
- model/provider substitutions;
- missing negatives;
- made-up universals, causes, objects, and “official” ontologies;
- bypassing control systems because they impede the LLM’s shortest path.

The desired language is operationalist, nominalist, process-oriented, and resistant to premature teleology. That is a salience goal, not something CB can deterministically prove about arbitrary prose.

